          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I Overview: An Attempt to Classify"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.185,
            0.311,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Acting humanly"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.066,
            0.285,
            0.817,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Turing Test",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", proposed by Alan Turing ( 1 950) . Turing ’ s definition of intelligent behavior as the ability to achieve human-level performance in all cognitive tasks ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.449,
            0.804,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The test involves an interrogator who interacts with one human and one machine. Within a given time the interrogator has to find out which of the two is the human, and which one the machine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.613,
            0.823,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is sue to solve in order to pas s the test using a terminal : natural language processing, knowledge representation automated reasoning, machine learning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.775,
            0.816,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "\u0000 Additional requirements for the “total Turing test” : computer vision, speech recognition, speech synthesis , robotics ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.0,
            0.954,
            0.351,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "IS 675 Peter ´ Molnar´ , 2003 (all rights reserved)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.829,
            0.954,
            0.885,
            0.98
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Slide 5"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.0,
            0.069,
            0.262,
            0.098
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I Overview: An Attempt to Classify"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.045,
            0.223,
            0.353,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thinking humanly"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.324,
            0.507,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "\u0000 Need to understand how humans think."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.392,
            0.199,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "\u0000 Methods :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.45,
            0.51,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "– catch our thoughts while they go by"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.508,
            0.416,
            0.546
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "– psychological experiments"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.574,
            0.793,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example: GPS , “General Problem Solver” (Newell and Simon 1 96 1 ) . Obj ective to compare the steps of the problem solving with the reasoning of human subj ects solving the same problem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.737,
            0.725,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cognitive Science",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " embraces computer models from AI and experimental methods from psychology."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.0,
            0.954,
            0.351,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
